1
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,634
[relaxing music playing]

2
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:24,774
[stewardess] Sir.

3
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:34,200
[young Javier] Ah, shit. Damn it!

4
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:36,953
- Sir, let me help you. Sorry, sir.
- [young Javier] No! Don't touch anything!

5
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,872
- Watch where you're stepping.
- [stewardess] I'm sorry.

6
00:00:38,955 --> 00:00:40,540
[young Andres] Why did you need
your bag anyway?

7
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:43,293
And why did you bring
Dad's records on our escape?

8
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:46,004
[young Javier] Papa spent years
collecting all of these.

9
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,506
Brother Rafael,
did you bring Dad's artworks?

10
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,341
Well, how else
are we going to pay for things?

11
00:00:50,425 --> 00:00:52,427
- [young Javier] Yeah.
- We're locked out of our accounts.

12
00:00:53,178 --> 00:00:55,597
If we can sell some of these artwork,

13
00:00:55,680 --> 00:00:57,348
things might be okay.

14
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:58,349
Thank you.

15
00:00:58,433 --> 00:01:00,060
[music continues]

16
00:01:00,977 --> 00:01:02,604
[young Andres] This is all you brought?

17
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:05,523
Be careful with those, will you?

18
00:01:06,149 --> 00:01:08,443
[young Andres] Records like these
are best kept on paper.

19
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:11,946
[groans] There's no money
in paperwork, okay?

20
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:13,823
It's not worth anything.

21
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:16,785
- [crashes]
- [stewardess yelps]

22
00:01:16,868 --> 00:01:18,620
[pants]

23
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:22,749
[young Javier] What the fuck?

24
00:01:25,210 --> 00:01:26,753
[thunder rumbling]

25
00:01:27,670 --> 00:01:28,755
[gasps]

26
00:01:30,423 --> 00:01:34,010
[breathes heavily]

27
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:37,972
[thunder rumbling]

28
00:01:40,892 --> 00:01:41,851
[grunts]

29
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:48,316
[young Javier] Holy shit. [panting]

30
00:01:49,901 --> 00:01:51,319
- [thunder rumbling]
- [all yelp]

31
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:54,280
- [men grunting]
- [seatbelt alarm beeping]

32
00:01:55,281 --> 00:01:57,408
- [young Rafael] Put your seatbelts on!
- In your seat, everyone.

33
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:58,660
Yeah.

34
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:00,078
We're experiencing turbulence.

35
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,248
[young Andres pants]

36
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:06,084
- [young Ramon] Javier! That's enough.
- Wait. I'm almost done!

37
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:07,669
- Yeah, yeah.
- [young Rafael] What happened?

38
00:02:09,462 --> 00:02:10,463
[young Ramon] Ah!

39
00:02:12,173 --> 00:02:13,341
[sobs]

40
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:16,136
- [young Ramon] Quick…
- [grunts]

41
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:17,554
Just sit down!

42
00:02:17,637 --> 00:02:18,763
- Sit down!
- [young Andres] Ramon!

43
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:20,014
[stewardess] Stop, sir!

44
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:23,017
- Please, stop!
- [young Ramon] Get a hold of yourself!

45
00:02:24,894 --> 00:02:26,771
Just… just stay calm, brother! Brother!

46
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:29,357
[young Javier] Ramon! [panting]

47
00:02:30,942 --> 00:02:32,777
[stewardess] Everybody, stay in your seat.

48
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,946
[young Ramon] Miss, you! Sit down too!

49
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:37,157
[stewardess] I need to talk to the pilot.

50
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,617
[breathing heavily]

51
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:42,704
No!

52
00:02:42,787 --> 00:02:44,164
[grunts]

53
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:48,168
[thunder rumbling]

54
00:02:48,251 --> 00:02:50,503
[pants]

55
00:02:53,047 --> 00:02:56,217
[ragged breathing]

56
00:02:57,552 --> 00:02:58,887
[explosion]

57
00:03:02,348 --> 00:03:04,475
[young Ramon breathing heavily]

58
00:03:11,733 --> 00:03:13,651
[water splashing]

59
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:21,284
[panting]

60
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:28,750
[breathes heavily]

61
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:48,061
[woman screaming]

62
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:49,687
[woman groans]

63
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,733
- [woman groaning in pain]
- [grunts]

64
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:58,279
[stewardess grunting]

65
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:03,368
No, no…

66
00:04:03,451 --> 00:04:04,953
Oh, oh-- Wait!

67
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:05,954
Don't!

68
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:08,081
[sobs]

69
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,834
[groans]

70
00:04:16,714 --> 00:04:18,258
[young Ramon] Violeta, wake up!

71
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,593
Someone help me! [grunts]

72
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:24,180
[stewardess groaning]

73
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:29,227
[both grunting]

74
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:32,063
- [stewardess screams]
- [groans]

75
00:04:36,484 --> 00:04:37,402
[young Ramon] Violeta!

76
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,990
[breathes heavily]

77
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,034
[breath trembling]

78
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:49,872
[pants]

79
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:59,716
[stewardess sobbing, groaning]

80
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:03,803
[young Ramon panting]

81
00:05:30,663 --> 00:05:32,373
[cries]

82
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:45,053
[young Rafael screaming] Ramon!

83
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:48,681
- [stewardess] Come now.
- Stay here!

84
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:50,183
Stay…

85
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:52,518
- [young Rafael screaming]
- [stewardess groaning]

86
00:05:54,312 --> 00:05:57,231
[young Rafael screaming] My leg!

87
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,693
- [young Rafael screams]
- [young Ramon] Rafael!

88
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:05,364
Rafael, hold on! Let me help!

89
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:08,201
[both screaming]

90
00:06:08,284 --> 00:06:09,660
[groans]

91
00:06:11,954 --> 00:06:13,247
[pants]

92
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:15,458
[grunts]

93
00:06:16,209 --> 00:06:17,126
[young Andres] Help!

94
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:20,254
- Help!
- [young Rafael] Where's Violeta?

95
00:06:20,338 --> 00:06:21,631
Find Violeta!

96
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,050
[young Ramon sobs] She's--

97
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:26,052
- She's gone.
- [groans]

98
00:06:26,969 --> 00:06:28,513
She's dead.

99
00:06:28,596 --> 00:06:30,389
- She's gone!
- [young Javier] Andres!

100
00:06:30,473 --> 00:06:31,891
[young Rafael] But my baby!

101
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:33,976
What about my son?

102
00:06:35,144 --> 00:06:36,562
Brother, I'll be back.

103
00:06:36,646 --> 00:06:37,939
I'll go look for help.

104
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,945
[ominous music playing]

105
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:07,552
[music swells]

106
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:21,399
[theme music playing]

107
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:27,632
BALARAW: BLOOD ISLAND

108
00:08:37,391 --> 00:08:40,978
[birds chirping in distance]

109
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:55,743
[Bulak] Sarge?

110
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:00,831
Sarge! [panting]

111
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:08,339
[both grunt]

112
00:09:08,422 --> 00:09:09,590
Sarge!

113
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:11,300
Sarge! Sarge.

114
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:19,809
[breathes heavily]

115
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,021
Are we alive?

116
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:27,149
- I think so.
- [Arturo panting]

117
00:09:28,484 --> 00:09:30,945
Nobody said hell was…

118
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,573
anything like this.

119
00:09:37,451 --> 00:09:41,956
Well, you sound pretty certain
that you'll be going to hell, huh?

120
00:09:44,125 --> 00:09:45,376
Oh, so you're not?

121
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,754
Hey, where are we?

122
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:52,300
I don't recognize any of this. [grunting]

123
00:09:53,509 --> 00:09:56,053
Yeah, neither do I, at all.

124
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:02,476
[sighs] I haven't even paid this off yet.

125
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:06,647
And where's Sabina? [pants]

126
00:10:14,238 --> 00:10:15,156
Uncle?

127
00:10:19,619 --> 00:10:20,536
Bulak!

128
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:25,625
Babe?

129
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:29,837
[sighs]

130
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:36,802
[leaves rustling]

131
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,763
[bird screeches]

132
00:10:42,850 --> 00:10:44,727
[panting]

133
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:52,234
[bird screeches]

134
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,261
[exhales]

135
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:23,140
[panting]

136
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,525
[breathes heavily]

137
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:37,029
[coughs]

138
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:59,135
[birds twittering]

139
00:12:00,636 --> 00:12:01,470
[Bulak] <i>Sabina?</i>

140
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:04,974
Sabina!

141
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:08,978
Is that my bag?

142
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,358
[panting]

143
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:20,406
Oh no, what happened?

144
00:12:20,489 --> 00:12:21,949
[Arturo] It's just wet.

145
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,411
I think we should look inland.

146
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:28,539
Come on.

147
00:12:31,876 --> 00:12:33,752
Oh, fuck you, Sarge.

148
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:56,692
[creature screeches distantly]

149
00:13:03,949 --> 00:13:05,242
[man 1] Let go of me!

150
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:06,869
[man 2] Stop them!

151
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:08,954
[man 1] Let me go, please!

152
00:13:10,873 --> 00:13:11,999
Let me go!

153
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:15,878
Fuck you!

154
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,007
[man 1 grunting]

155
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,135
[man 1 grunts]

156
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:25,221
[Sabina panting]

157
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:27,556
[man 2] Stand up.

158
00:13:30,643 --> 00:13:31,560
Give it to me.

159
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,498
[breath trembling]

160
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:57,169
- [man 1 screaming]
- [Sabina grunts]

161
00:13:57,253 --> 00:14:01,048
- [breath trembling]
- [breathes heavily]

162
00:14:02,550 --> 00:14:05,010
[panting]

163
00:14:05,511 --> 00:14:07,805
[man 1 screaming]

164
00:14:08,389 --> 00:14:11,183
- [breath trembling]
- [suspenseful music playing]

165
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:20,317
[gasps]

166
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:31,745
[Sabina] Ah! What are you doing?

167
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:32,705
Leave me alone!

168
00:14:32,788 --> 00:14:33,914
[man 3] Come on, get in there!

169
00:14:33,998 --> 00:14:35,040
[screams]

170
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:37,668
[Sabina] Wait!

171
00:14:37,751 --> 00:14:38,627
Just wait.

172
00:14:40,212 --> 00:14:43,340
Sir, I'm looking
for my mother, that's all.

173
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:46,302
Rebecca. My mother's name is Rebecca.

174
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,470
Have you seen her?

175
00:14:51,056 --> 00:14:52,057
Is she here?

176
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:54,518
Hey, wait!

177
00:14:54,602 --> 00:14:55,728
Don't leave me here!

178
00:14:55,811 --> 00:14:57,187
Stop! Come back!

179
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:58,814
Hey!

180
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:01,734
Who are you?

181
00:15:03,402 --> 00:15:05,321
[creature screeches distantly]

182
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:16,749
Sir?

183
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:18,459
Where are we?

184
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:21,879
Sir?

185
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:25,716
[man 4] Where? No one knows where.

186
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:29,303
[Sabina] Perhaps you might know my mother.

187
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:31,764
Her name's Rebecca.

188
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,187
[man 4] Hmm.

189
00:15:38,604 --> 00:15:39,688
No, lady.

190
00:15:41,523 --> 00:15:43,943
We don't know anyone called Rebecca.

191
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:47,947
You're the only woman we've seen here.

192
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:54,078
How long have you been in here?

193
00:15:56,163 --> 00:15:57,122
A few weeks.

194
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:00,960
A few months. Lost…

195
00:16:01,627 --> 00:16:02,753
I lost track.

196
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:07,299
I don't really know.

197
00:16:11,136 --> 00:16:15,015
I heard the man outside
say he's been here for decades.

198
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:20,062
Maybe he knows where your Rebecca is.

199
00:16:23,774 --> 00:16:26,819
[clattering, door creaks]

200
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,407
[Sabina] Let go of me! [groans]

201
00:16:32,908 --> 00:16:34,368
Where are you taking me?

202
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,828
[ominous music playing]

203
00:16:35,911 --> 00:16:37,955
You're hurting me! Let go!

204
00:16:44,253 --> 00:16:45,254
[grunts]

205
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:36,680
Leave us.

206
00:17:51,653 --> 00:17:52,821
Rebecca is your mother?

207
00:17:55,866 --> 00:17:56,867
Yes.

208
00:17:57,618 --> 00:17:58,494
Do you know her?

209
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:01,413
How old are you?

210
00:18:03,665 --> 00:18:04,583
Why?

211
00:18:10,506 --> 00:18:11,423
Twenty-five.

212
00:18:24,103 --> 00:18:26,188
It's good to see you, at last.

213
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:33,487
I'm Sabina.

214
00:18:36,198 --> 00:18:37,157
Sabina.

215
00:18:39,618 --> 00:18:41,954
It's so good to meet you, Sabina.

216
00:18:56,969 --> 00:18:58,095
Sabina.

217
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:02,808
I am your father.

218
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:05,894
I am Ramon.

219
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,730
[music swells]

220
00:19:08,814 --> 00:19:10,482
[pants]

221
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:44,975
Let's not take any risks.

222
00:19:46,602 --> 00:19:48,187
What do you mean?

223
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:49,605
It's just an old lady.

224
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:52,065
Oh, I see.

225
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:54,318
Because she's a woman?

226
00:19:54,401 --> 00:19:55,569
And because she's old?

227
00:19:56,695 --> 00:19:57,613
Go figure.

228
00:19:58,572 --> 00:20:00,199
[Arturo] What is it with you?

229
00:20:00,282 --> 00:20:02,284
Why do you disagree with everything?

230
00:20:02,367 --> 00:20:04,036
I'm just trying to educate you.

231
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:05,746
[Arturo] This is not
the right time for that.

232
00:20:05,829 --> 00:20:07,956
- We need to work together.
- [Bulak] Typical man.

233
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:11,543
[Arturo] We need to be a team
because we're all alone here.

234
00:20:11,627 --> 00:20:12,628
Are you paying attention

235
00:20:12,711 --> 00:20:13,670
- to what I'm saying?
- Look!

236
00:20:13,754 --> 00:20:15,047
- [Arturo] Are you listening?
- Look!

237
00:20:19,468 --> 00:20:20,552
[stammers] Hello?

238
00:20:25,182 --> 00:20:26,099
Ma'am.

239
00:20:28,894 --> 00:20:30,812
What is this place? Where are we?

240
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:33,398
You're new here, aren't you?

241
00:20:36,193 --> 00:20:37,486
You should be careful.

242
00:20:37,569 --> 00:20:39,029
Don't let them find you here.

243
00:20:43,492 --> 00:20:45,118
What are you saying? Careful of who?

244
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,996
You don't know.

245
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:50,123
You're new.

246
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:52,751
You don't understand the danger.

247
00:20:53,752 --> 00:20:56,463
No one ever leaves this island alive.

248
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,757
We must find Aunt Becca.

249
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:02,094
Rebecca?

250
00:21:03,136 --> 00:21:03,971
Yes, Rebecca.

251
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:07,849
It's like I told you.

252
00:21:09,101 --> 00:21:11,853
There is no one
who ever leaves this place alive.

253
00:21:16,608 --> 00:21:18,193
Go away! Run!

254
00:21:18,277 --> 00:21:19,695
Leave this place now!

255
00:21:19,778 --> 00:21:20,946
Go, hide!

256
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:23,198
[Bulak] Come on, let's go! Hurry!

257
00:21:33,583 --> 00:21:34,626
What are you doing here?

258
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:37,087
[old woman] Don't you touch my things.

259
00:21:37,713 --> 00:21:39,881
[man] Keep a lookout. There are intruders.

260
00:21:54,438 --> 00:21:56,106
[fire crackling]

261
00:21:58,150 --> 00:22:00,527
[wind howling]

262
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:15,125
[eerie music playing]

263
00:22:33,393 --> 00:22:34,311
[Ramon] Sabina.

264
00:22:35,771 --> 00:22:36,688
Let's go.

265
00:22:52,704 --> 00:22:53,622
Come in.

266
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:02,130
This is your house?

267
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:03,924
Our house, Sabina.

268
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,009
It's ours.

269
00:23:11,389 --> 00:23:12,265
Let's go.

270
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:23,151
[music fades]

271
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:26,738
Come in, come in.

272
00:23:33,912 --> 00:23:35,205
Wait there just a second.

273
00:24:04,401 --> 00:24:05,360
Sabina.

274
00:24:10,949 --> 00:24:12,784
This is my brother, Rafael.

275
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:14,452
He's our eldest.

276
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,416
[Rafael] Keep still now.

277
00:24:21,001 --> 00:24:22,043
[grunts]

278
00:24:26,173 --> 00:24:27,424
Where are we exactly?

279
00:24:29,426 --> 00:24:31,595
Balaraw is what they call this island.

280
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:33,263
"They"?

281
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:35,682
[Ramon] Yes, the people you saw earlier.

282
00:24:35,765 --> 00:24:37,475
They're the locals here.

283
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:39,060
And you guys?

284
00:24:40,228 --> 00:24:41,980
Oh, us?

285
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:43,398
We're just guests here.

286
00:24:44,399 --> 00:24:45,859
But we came to love it a lot.

287
00:24:47,194 --> 00:24:48,528
So, we decided to stay.

288
00:24:50,697 --> 00:24:51,990
[groans]

289
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,619
This could need stitches.

290
00:24:58,747 --> 00:25:00,373
So, you're a doctor now?

291
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:01,374
[Sabina] Nurse.

292
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:04,044
[groans softly]

293
00:25:13,553 --> 00:25:14,971
So was my wife.

294
00:25:16,056 --> 00:25:17,349
[clatters]

295
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:20,852
You don't need stitches.

296
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:24,439
You just need to keep this wound clean.

297
00:25:26,566 --> 00:25:27,776
And you're good.

298
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:32,864
Excellent.

299
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:33,865
Time to go.

300
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:37,911
Go?

301
00:25:37,994 --> 00:25:39,079
To your room.

302
00:25:40,163 --> 00:25:41,289
You should be resting.

303
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:10,151
Are you really my father?

304
00:26:11,653 --> 00:26:12,570
I think so.

305
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:15,657
You think so?

306
00:26:19,452 --> 00:26:20,787
Twenty-five years ago,

307
00:26:21,997 --> 00:26:23,707
that's when I first knew Rebecca.

308
00:26:23,790 --> 00:26:25,625
And you're 25 now, right?

309
00:26:28,169 --> 00:26:30,046
You said you never knew your father.

310
00:26:33,466 --> 00:26:34,843
You never tried to find him?

311
00:26:35,552 --> 00:26:36,469
Of course, I did.

312
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:43,435
I've always felt different,
like something was missing in my life.

313
00:26:47,147 --> 00:26:49,524
I understand how you feel.

314
00:26:50,233 --> 00:26:51,776
I've always felt that way.

315
00:26:53,153 --> 00:26:54,154
And so…

316
00:26:55,864 --> 00:26:57,991
the Lord is the only one I trust.

317
00:26:59,284 --> 00:27:02,037
After all, there's no one else
to turn to, is there?

318
00:27:03,913 --> 00:27:04,956
Where is Rebecca?

319
00:27:05,749 --> 00:27:08,168
[groans] She just left,

320
00:27:09,377 --> 00:27:10,628
right before you arrived.

321
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:12,797
Actually, what occurred is,

322
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:14,507
we ran out of clean water here,

323
00:27:15,717 --> 00:27:18,386
so she left in search of a fresh source.

324
00:27:19,804 --> 00:27:21,765
I shouldn't worry. She'll be back soon.

325
00:27:22,932 --> 00:27:24,726
Why did she want to come here?

326
00:27:25,685 --> 00:27:27,062
This is her true home,

327
00:27:27,645 --> 00:27:29,230
where she naturally belongs.

328
00:27:31,900 --> 00:27:33,526
She didn't tell you any of that?

329
00:27:38,865 --> 00:27:40,575
[eerie music playing]

330
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:46,373
I came here with another girl
and also another man.

331
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:49,125
Have you seen either of them at all?

332
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:50,502
No. I'm sorry.

333
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:53,004
But the Lord will not fail us.

334
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:56,591
There are people
on the other side of this island.

335
00:27:56,674 --> 00:27:57,884
They will look for them.

336
00:27:57,967 --> 00:27:59,302
You must have faith.

337
00:28:00,387 --> 00:28:02,138
The Lord never lets us down.

338
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:07,685
[music continues]

339
00:28:20,907 --> 00:28:22,784
Okay. You rest now.

340
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:37,757
[bats squeaking]

341
00:28:37,841 --> 00:28:39,551
[Arturo] Fuck, this is soaked.

342
00:28:41,469 --> 00:28:42,929
[Arturo blowing]

343
00:28:43,012 --> 00:28:44,013
[water dripping]

344
00:28:49,477 --> 00:28:51,646
Do you think
we'll be safe enough here, Sarge?

345
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:53,898
- [Arturo] It's "Captain."
- Huh?

346
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:56,901
You know that I'm a captain,
so why call me Sarge?

347
00:28:56,985 --> 00:28:58,153
[Bulak] Because you're a bully.

348
00:28:59,279 --> 00:29:00,613
Those two men,

349
00:29:00,697 --> 00:29:02,949
I have a bad feeling about them.

350
00:29:03,032 --> 00:29:04,451
Plus, they were armed.

351
00:29:05,034 --> 00:29:06,536
I can take the first watch now.

352
00:29:07,412 --> 00:29:08,621
Then, we'll take turns.

353
00:29:09,539 --> 00:29:10,582
[sighs]

354
00:29:12,625 --> 00:29:13,752
[gasps]

355
00:29:13,835 --> 00:29:15,253
Sarge, it's working!

356
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:24,471
- [sighs] Still no signal, though.
- [Arturo] Ah.

357
00:29:24,554 --> 00:29:25,805
What do you really expect?

358
00:29:27,891 --> 00:29:30,101
You can get some sleep.
I'll take the first watch.

359
00:29:30,727 --> 00:29:32,020
I'll do it.

360
00:29:32,103 --> 00:29:34,105
[Bulak] It's fine. I can't sleep anyway.

361
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:49,996
Tomorrow, we'll leave here
and we'll find Sabina.

362
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:51,539
[moody music playing]

363
00:29:56,169 --> 00:29:57,504
[water dripping]

364
00:30:18,149 --> 00:30:19,859
[low trilling sound]

365
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:24,322
- [squelching]
- [creature growls]

366
00:30:28,034 --> 00:30:28,910
[creature screeches]

367
00:30:31,913 --> 00:30:33,164
[creature trilling]

368
00:30:34,165 --> 00:30:35,333
[wood creaks]

369
00:30:50,348 --> 00:30:51,307
[sighs]

370
00:30:51,391 --> 00:30:52,392
[floor creaking]

371
00:31:05,113 --> 00:31:06,281
[footsteps approaching]

372
00:31:08,074 --> 00:31:09,784
Ah, you're awake, are you?

373
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:11,619
Tea?

374
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:13,538
There's a woman in my room.

375
00:31:13,621 --> 00:31:16,207
Ah, that would be Diwa.

376
00:31:16,291 --> 00:31:17,667
I asked her to rouse you.

377
00:31:18,918 --> 00:31:21,254
Oh, wait. You've not eaten at all?

378
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:23,923
I'm so sorry I didn't offer you
anything last night.

379
00:31:24,841 --> 00:31:26,175
You must be starving.

380
00:31:26,259 --> 00:31:27,802
Let's get you some food.

381
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:36,060
[birds chirping]

382
00:31:45,778 --> 00:31:47,238
It's a small place we have.

383
00:31:49,073 --> 00:31:51,034
Everyone has their own job to do.

384
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:55,496
So we can live well
in peace and happiness.

385
00:32:03,087 --> 00:32:06,049
You see, most of our things
are recycled here.

386
00:32:08,134 --> 00:32:09,802
Some were carried by the sea,

387
00:32:11,888 --> 00:32:14,766
other things fell from the sky. [chuckles]

388
00:32:20,813 --> 00:32:22,231
[man] Just a little now.

389
00:32:23,858 --> 00:32:25,068
It just needs a trickle.

390
00:32:26,277 --> 00:32:27,278
Doing a good job.

391
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:29,822
That's a good boy.

392
00:32:32,408 --> 00:32:33,618
Good job.

393
00:32:33,701 --> 00:32:36,037
No need to drown it, is there?

394
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:39,165
A little bit of water could go a long way.

395
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:47,840
[Ramon] Andres.

396
00:32:51,177 --> 00:32:52,136
Meet Sabina.

397
00:32:53,513 --> 00:32:56,766
Sabina, this is Andres, my brother.

398
00:32:58,017 --> 00:32:58,851
Older brother.

399
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:01,562
Indeed. [chuckles]

400
00:33:03,064 --> 00:33:05,441
Brother, do you happen
to have food in there?

401
00:33:05,525 --> 00:33:06,359
She's very hungry.

402
00:33:07,318 --> 00:33:08,403
I have vegetables.

403
00:33:08,486 --> 00:33:11,447
Unfortunately, our meat supply
is a bit limited here.

404
00:33:12,198 --> 00:33:13,866
Whatever you have is fine.

405
00:33:14,742 --> 00:33:15,660
Andres,

406
00:33:16,661 --> 00:33:18,663
we have meat enough to share.

407
00:33:19,330 --> 00:33:22,083
Let's enjoy it now
that we have a special guest.

408
00:33:23,376 --> 00:33:24,544
If you say so.

409
00:33:24,627 --> 00:33:26,754
[mysterious music playing]

410
00:33:30,925 --> 00:33:33,636
[creatures screeching]

411
00:33:33,720 --> 00:33:34,762
[gasps]

412
00:33:44,689 --> 00:33:45,606
Bulak?

413
00:33:47,316 --> 00:33:48,359
Bulak!

414
00:33:51,612 --> 00:33:52,488
Bulak!

415
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:57,243
Bulak!

416
00:34:09,422 --> 00:34:10,256
Bulak!

417
00:34:22,143 --> 00:34:23,728
[water dripping]

418
00:34:38,493 --> 00:34:40,620
Bulak, what are you doing here?

419
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:43,122
[Bulak] I thought I heard something.

420
00:34:43,831 --> 00:34:46,167
Wait! It could be a wild animal.

421
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,376
- [Bulak] Over here.
- Wait.

422
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,170
Be careful.

423
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:50,463
[Bulak] It came from here.

424
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:55,343
[mysterious music playing]

425
00:34:56,594 --> 00:34:57,762
[Bulak] Are you seeing this?

426
00:35:01,099 --> 00:35:02,683
[trilling sounds]

427
00:35:07,980 --> 00:35:10,233
[Bulak panting]

428
00:35:11,859 --> 00:35:13,986
[creatures screeching]

429
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:17,073
Let's go!

430
00:35:19,867 --> 00:35:21,077
Bulak.

431
00:35:21,160 --> 00:35:21,994
Bulak.

432
00:35:23,746 --> 00:35:24,747
Let's go!

433
00:35:31,045 --> 00:35:32,130
[Bulak] Look at this.

434
00:35:34,090 --> 00:35:35,133
- [squelches]
- [Bulak gasps]

435
00:35:38,427 --> 00:35:40,513
[Bulak] Fuck! Let's get out of here.

436
00:35:40,596 --> 00:35:41,514
Come on, hurry!

437
00:35:41,597 --> 00:35:43,266
[Arturo] Why did you touch it like that?

438
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:47,228
[panting]

439
00:35:48,396 --> 00:35:50,231
- Hey, wait! Where are we going?
- [Bulak] Where else?

440
00:35:50,314 --> 00:35:51,399
We've got to find Sabina.

441
00:35:51,482 --> 00:35:52,942
This place is dangerous.

442
00:35:53,025 --> 00:35:55,486
While you were sleeping,
I saw smoke over there.

443
00:35:55,570 --> 00:35:57,280
Maybe that's where they all live.

444
00:35:58,656 --> 00:35:59,907
[tense music playing]

445
00:35:59,991 --> 00:36:03,202
Lord God, we thank You
for these blessings.

446
00:36:04,328 --> 00:36:06,789
Not just for the food You have given us,

447
00:36:08,666 --> 00:36:10,001
But we thank You for

448
00:36:11,502 --> 00:36:14,255
our new friend who has visited us here

449
00:36:14,338 --> 00:36:15,631
on our special island.

450
00:36:17,758 --> 00:36:20,094
This, our island paradise,

451
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:24,557
which has brought us so much joy

452
00:36:25,224 --> 00:36:27,852
and a perfect home for us all.

453
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:33,149
One we thought could only possibly exist

454
00:36:33,941 --> 00:36:35,985
in Your divine presence,

455
00:36:36,068 --> 00:36:37,528
we thank You for this.

456
00:36:40,198 --> 00:36:41,991
For keeping watch over us

457
00:36:43,117 --> 00:36:44,869
and protecting us as You do.

458
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:47,788
Amen.

459
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:51,250
Eat up.

460
00:37:11,812 --> 00:37:13,022
[Ramon] You're not hungry?

461
00:37:53,938 --> 00:37:55,773
We've been walking for ages.

462
00:38:06,158 --> 00:38:09,328
Hey, you must stop scratching at that.

463
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:12,957
[Bulak] Ow!

464
00:38:13,040 --> 00:38:14,166
[grunts]

465
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:18,170
Ah!

466
00:38:18,254 --> 00:38:19,171
Just wait.

467
00:38:21,007 --> 00:38:22,300
[hisses]

468
00:38:31,058 --> 00:38:32,768
Can I ask you something?

469
00:38:34,020 --> 00:38:35,062
Could I stop you?

470
00:38:37,648 --> 00:38:39,483
Do you have feelings for Aunt Becca?

471
00:38:41,527 --> 00:38:42,445
Feelings?

472
00:38:43,112 --> 00:38:44,030
Why do you ask?

473
00:38:45,531 --> 00:38:46,949
Whatever gave you that idea?

474
00:38:47,575 --> 00:38:49,035
It's just that--

475
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:50,578
It's a hassle for you.

476
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,247
All this, at your age?

477
00:38:54,165 --> 00:38:55,082
No offense.

478
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:00,254
So, I figured
that you must really love her

479
00:39:00,338 --> 00:39:02,548
to be so dedicated to finding her.

480
00:39:04,300 --> 00:39:05,384
I do love Rebecca.

481
00:39:06,427 --> 00:39:10,097
I consider her as part
of my family, and Sabina.

482
00:39:10,181 --> 00:39:12,725
Then why didn't you ever
come looking for her?

483
00:39:13,684 --> 00:39:16,270
You've known for a long time
she was on this island.

484
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:21,942
I couldn't do what she did to Sabina.

485
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:25,529
I had responsibilities.

486
00:39:27,198 --> 00:39:29,450
You really see her as family, don't you?

487
00:39:29,533 --> 00:39:31,369
Just don't mistake me for family.

488
00:39:32,244 --> 00:39:33,412
You got that?

489
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:37,291
Well, there you go.

490
00:39:38,751 --> 00:39:39,919
Oh, don't mention it.

491
00:39:41,337 --> 00:39:42,254
It was nothing.

492
00:39:43,339 --> 00:39:44,548
Let's go.

493
00:39:46,050 --> 00:39:47,593
Hey, wait, Sarge, I just gotta pee.

494
00:39:47,676 --> 00:39:49,011
I won't be long.

495
00:39:53,974 --> 00:39:55,893
[birds chirping]

496
00:39:58,562 --> 00:40:01,107
[ominous music playing]

497
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:56,704
[inaudible]

498
00:41:12,678 --> 00:41:14,388
Are they talking about my friends?

499
00:41:15,222 --> 00:41:16,140
[Ramon] No.

500
00:41:18,058 --> 00:41:21,228
If we hear anything about them,
you'll be the first to know. I promise.

501
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:24,482
It's probably some issue
at the campsite or something.

502
00:41:25,691 --> 00:41:26,984
[Sabina] Where I was locked up?

503
00:41:28,611 --> 00:41:29,445
[Ramon] You know,

504
00:41:31,071 --> 00:41:32,448
we have a system here.

505
00:41:35,034 --> 00:41:39,705
There are some who come here
who don't have, mmm, such good intentions.

506
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:42,666
When they're done proving
that they're not here to cause trouble,

507
00:41:43,292 --> 00:41:48,339
then they can choose
to live with us or they're free to go.

508
00:41:49,256 --> 00:41:50,174
It's that simple.

509
00:41:52,218 --> 00:41:53,928
Of course, your case is different.

510
00:41:54,887 --> 00:41:57,640
You're my daughter,
so I know I can trust you.

511
00:41:59,934 --> 00:42:01,519
It's easy, you know?

512
00:42:06,649 --> 00:42:08,817
What makes you so sure you can trust me?

513
00:42:12,196 --> 00:42:13,864
[sighs] Come.

514
00:42:40,182 --> 00:42:42,142
This is when I first met Rebecca.

515
00:42:43,269 --> 00:42:44,395
Hmm.

516
00:42:48,899 --> 00:42:50,192
[Ramon chuckles]

517
00:42:50,276 --> 00:42:52,653
I have no proof
that you're really my daughter.

518
00:42:57,199 --> 00:42:59,159
[Sabina] Who are all these people here?

519
00:42:59,243 --> 00:43:01,787
Well, they're all marine
biology researchers.

520
00:43:03,080 --> 00:43:07,710
But instead of doing research,
they all got lost here on this island.

521
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:09,295
[scoffs]

522
00:43:10,170 --> 00:43:11,046
Who is this here?

523
00:43:12,047 --> 00:43:14,883
[Ramon] Oh, that's Vedasto,
Rebecca's older brother.

524
00:43:14,967 --> 00:43:16,677
She never talked about him?

525
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:21,890
There's so much she hid from me.

526
00:43:25,603 --> 00:43:27,771
It's like I never knew the real her.

527
00:43:28,522 --> 00:43:31,483
It's never too late, you know,
to get to know your parents.

528
00:43:32,651 --> 00:43:35,446
You're lucky
that we're still alive. [chuckles]

529
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:42,161
My brothers and I,
we don't have our parents anymore to love.

530
00:43:47,416 --> 00:43:48,334
But maybe…

531
00:43:50,502 --> 00:43:53,589
not all parents
earn the love of their children.

532
00:43:56,300 --> 00:43:59,094
I expect some abuse their kids,

533
00:44:01,055 --> 00:44:03,474
and don't care at all
about their children.

534
00:44:09,563 --> 00:44:11,440
I swore to myself that I…

535
00:44:13,776 --> 00:44:16,904
I couldn't ever do that to my own child.

536
00:44:16,987 --> 00:44:19,615
[ominous music playing]

537
00:44:56,902 --> 00:44:58,320
[sighs]

538
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:01,615
[sighs wearily]

539
00:45:09,164 --> 00:45:10,374
[grunts]

540
00:45:22,678 --> 00:45:23,595
Ooh.

541
00:45:27,433 --> 00:45:30,602
[music continues]

542
00:45:49,121 --> 00:45:50,038
Sarge?

543
00:46:09,183 --> 00:46:11,185
[Bulak screaming]

544
00:46:12,019 --> 00:46:14,354
[suspenseful music playing]

545
00:46:45,969 --> 00:46:47,137
Let her go!

546
00:46:50,599 --> 00:46:51,600
[Bulak whimpers]

547
00:46:52,893 --> 00:46:54,770
I said, let her go.

548
